.SH "نام (NAME)"
timew-export \- export tracked time in JSON
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
.nf
\fBtimew export\fP [ \fI<id>\fP\fB...\fP | ([\fI<range>\fP] [\fI<tag>\fP\fB...\fP]) ]
.fi
.br
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Exports all the tracked time in JSON format.
.sp
Supply either a list of interval IDs, or a range and/or tag filter (see \fBtimew\-ranges\fP(7) and \fBtimew\-tags\fP(1)) to export only a subset of intervals.
.sp
The data is exported as a JSON array of interval objects, each containing the start time, end time, current id, tags, and annotation of the interval, if present.
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.sp
\fBExport all intervals\fP
.RS 4
.sp
Calling the \f(CRexport\fP command without any arguments exports all tracked intervals in JSON format:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
$ timew export
[
{"id":2,"start":"20231001T103000Z","end":"20231001T120000Z","tags":["work"],"annotation":"Project work"},
{"id":1,"start":"20231001T090000Z","end":"20231001T100000Z","tags":["work"],"annotation":"Morning meeting"},
]
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
In this example, only two intervals are present in the database.
The output is sorted by start time, with the oldest interval first.
.RE
.sp
\fBExport intervals filtered by range and tag\fP
.RS 4
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
$ timew export from 2016\-01\-01 for 3wks tag1
\&...
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.RE
.sp
\fBExport intervals by their ids\fP
.RS 4
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
$ timew export @1 @3 @7
\&...
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.RE